From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:16:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 072/148] hjviewer: review fixes, home lane

U22: a PC card opens its menu on a right-click's release (onSecondaryTapUp)
instead of its press. Tap-down fires after 100 ms even for a recognizer
that later loses, so a right-click held on the card's more button opened
the card's menu and the button's; tap-up fires only for the winner, the
button's own detector. The ID card's more button, activated from the
keyboard, opens its menu under the button instead of the window's corner,
and its Change ID entry needs the settings' Security tab, as
switch2page does nothing without it.

U57: on a phone the empty My PCs list and a search that matches nothing
scroll inside the refresh indicator, so pulling them down refreshes the
list; on a 360 dp phone the bar's refresh is under "more". The connect
button next to the ID field is a labelled button for screen readers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
